title: 'cumulus: fix V3 scheduling parent picking, wait for RC tip'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    At relay parent offset 0 the V3 scheduling parent is the last
    finished-slot relay block, which may have same-height siblings; picking
    among them from the local view is arrival-order luck, and building on
    the losing sibling wastes the slot. The collator now waits for a relay
    block of the current production slot, whose parent hash names the
    canonical scheduling parent. The walk-back is also bounded by the slot
    timer's production slot instead of a second wall-clock read: the slot
    timer is the single source of truth for the current slot.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
